  "dyadic_representation_qualification": "The C I record uses implicit exponent -100. The executable decoder validates sign/domain bits and order. Canonical inputs match exact old negation; arbitrary old coarser representations use SameValues endpoint-rational equality. Zero represents original finSumZero by endpoint values; field equality is not claimed.",
  "comparison_domain_note": "Signed decoder validates bit flags but accepts raw negative zero. Add/mul/negation mathematics remains valid on raw Signed values. Actual sc/qc sign-first comparison must additionally require ZeroNormalized(mag=0 implies neg=false), established by every smake constructor output; not a mismatch in proof-bearing normalized use. SignedNormalization proves make/add/mul/negated normalization; sa_math includes its normalized output."
